# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
.venv*/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
dist/
build/

# --- Node / frontend ---
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/coverage/
.pnpm-store/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Env and secrets ---
# .env.example is the only committed dotenv file; every other .env* is local.
.env
.env.*
!deploy/.env.example

# --- Editors and OS ---
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Generated / local data, never source ---
# Ad hoc exports (FR-78) and release artefacts are runtime output, not repo content.
/exports/
/releases/
# Default output directory for the transform CLI (issue #23) - defect reports in
# both machine- and human-readable form. Regenerated from the source workbook on
# every run, and named after whichever workbook was passed in, so committing it
# would just be noise that goes stale.
/out/
# docs/requirements/traceability.md (F-5) used to be committed the same way
# docs/api/openapi.json is, but unlike openapi.json it diverges byte-for-byte
# between any two branches with different @pytest.mark.req markers or
# requirements.yaml edits - every cherry-pick or rebase across such branches
# hit a merge conflict in a file neither side cared about the content of
# (issue #126). CI's `traceability` job (docs.yml) still regenerates and
# validates it every run; it's just an uploaded build artefact now, not a
# tracked file - run `uv run python scripts/traceability_check.py` locally to
# produce it on demand.
/docs/requirements/traceability.md

# --- Local override files ---
docker-compose.override.yml
*.local.yml
P1-SEQUENCING.md

# --- Claude Code local state ---
# Session/plugin-local data (e.g. the healthcare plugin's data/healthcare/documents/
# sqlite db) and settings.local.json are per-machine, never repo content.
.claude/
